--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY DATA NOTICE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This licence covers the SOURCE CODE AND DOCUMENTATION IN THIS REPOSITORY ONLY.
It does not cover, and cannot grant rights to, the UNSW-NB15 dataset.

The UNSW-NB15 dataset was created by Dr Nour Moustafa and Dr Jill Slay at the
Australian Centre for Cyber Security (ACCS), UNSW Canberra. It is distributed by
its authors for research and academic purposes with attribution. No dataset
files are committed to this repository; `src/data_loader.py` retrieves them at
runtime from public sources.

Anyone using this project must comply with the dataset's own terms and cite:

  Moustafa, N. and Slay, J. (2015). UNSW-NB15: a comprehensive data set for
  network intrusion detection systems (UNSW-NB15 network data set). Military
  Communications and Information Systems Conference (MilCIS), IEEE.

  Moustafa, N. and Slay, J. (2016). The evaluation of Network Anomaly Detection
  Systems: Statistical analysis of the UNSW-NB15 data set and the comparison
  with the KDD99 data set. Information Security Journal: A Global Perspective,
  25(1-3), 18-31.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
INTENDED USE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project is an educational and research artefact. The trained models are
not fit for use as a standalone production intrusion-detection system. See the
"Limitations" section of README.md and reports/Final_Project_Report.md before
relying on any output.
